(3) The controller of the examination shall be a full-time olficei of the University andshall be responsible for all the mattiars connected with the conduction ofexamination and pet-form such other duties as may be prescribed.{4) The controller of the examination shall be appoinled for a renewable term of three(03) years.Provided thal the board of Governors may, on the advice of the Rector, terminate theappointment of the Controlter of the Examination on the ground of inefficiency ormisconduct in accidence with prescribed procedure.
17.(1)
Oirector Planning & Development: -There shall be a Director Planning and Development of the University to beappointed by the Board of Govemors on the recommendation of the Syndicatefor a period of three (03) years {once renewable) on such terms & conditions asmay be prescribed.The minimum experience as well as the professional and academic qualificationsnece$ary for the appointment to the post of Director Planning & Developmentshall be prescribed.The Director Planning & Developmenl shall be responsible for all mattersconnected with planning and development and perform such other duties as maybe prescribed.
{2)
(r)
(4) The Director planning & Development shall:
(i) Prepare short and long-term ptans and development programs to meetvision,.goals and priorities set by the University managemenuBoard ofGovernors,(iD Conducl comprehensive review, assessment, and analysis ofdevelopment planning process (project identification, appraisal, selection,implementation, and monitoring) and mechanism:(iii) Develop a strategy for improving development planning processes andmechanisms based on findings of the situalion analysis:(iv) Provide technical support in developing proiect proposals and PCs-1 forthe University;
Prepalation of the PCl, PC-ll, PC lll, PC lV, and PC-V
Preparation of cash work and activity plan;
Preparation of quarterly expenditure statements;
(v)(vi)(vii)(viii)
Preparation of monthly and quarterly progress reports;
