Provided that effort shall be made, without compromising of quality orqualificalion, to give fuir representation to women on the Board of Governors.Provided further that as regards the Uriversity Teachers specifled in clause (h) ofsub-section (1), the Board of Govemors shall prescribe a procedure forappointment on the basis of elections that provide for voting by the varicuscategories of University Teachers. Provided also that the Board of Govemors n ayalternatively prescribe that appointment of University Teachers to the Board ofGovernors shall also be in the manner provided by this sub-section for thepersons specified in clauses (0 to (S) of sub-section(1)(4) Members of the Board of Governors, other than ex officio members, st,allhold office for three yesrs. One-third of the members, other than ex offi:lomembers, of the First Board of Govemors, lo be determined by lot, shall rel irefrom office on the expiration of one year from the date of apPointment by:heChancellor. One half of the remaining members, other than ex officio memb€rs,of the First Board of Governors, to be determined by lot, shall retire from oflice onthe expiration of tvvo years from the date of appointment and the remaining otre-half, other than ex officio members, shall retire from office on the expiration of .hethird year:Provided that no person, other than an ex officio member, may serve onthe Board of Governors for more than two consecutive terms:Provided further that the University Teachers appointed to the Board ofGovernors may not serve for two consecutive terms.(5) The Board of Governors shall meet at least twice in a calendar yerar.(6) Service on the Board of Governors shall be on honorary ba 3is.However, actual expenses may be reimbursed as prescribed.(7) The Regishar shall be the Secretary ofthe Board of Governors.(8) ln the absence of the Chancellor, meetings of the Board ofGovernors shall be presided over by such member' not being anemployee of the University or the Govemment, as the Chance llormay, from time to lime, nominate. The member so nominated srallbe the convener of the Board of Governors,
(9) Unless otherwise prescribed by this Act, alt decisions of the Boardof Governors shall be taken on the basis of the opinion of a majorityof the members present. ln the event of the members being evenlydivided on any matter the person presiding over the meeting shallhave a casting vote.(10) The quorum for a meeting of the Board of Governors shall be twothirds of ils membership, a fraction belng counted as one.
