Provided that regulations regarding incidental to matters contained in sub-clauses (0and (h) shall not be submitted to the board of governors without the prior approval of thesyndicate.(2) Regulations shafl be proposed by the Academic council and shall be submitted tothe board of governors which may approve them or withhold approval or refer them backto the academic council for reconsideration. A regulation proposed by the academiccouncil shall not be effective untess it reeeives the approval of the board of govemors.32. Amendment and repeat of statues and regurations. - the procedure for addingto amending or repealing the statues and the regulations shall be the same as thaiprescribed respectively for framing or making stalues and regulations.33. Rules:-(1) the authorities and the other bodies of the university may make rules,consistent with this Act, statues or the regulations, to r€gulate any matter relating to theaffairs of the university which has not been provided for by this Act or that is not requiredto be regulated by statues or regulations, including rules to regulate the conduct ofbusiness and the time and place of meetings and related matters.(2) Rules shall become effective upon approval by the syndicate.
Chapter VlUniversity Funds34. university fund.- the university shall have a fund to which shalt be credited itsincome from fees, charges donations, trusts, bequests, endowments, contributions,grants and all other sources.35' Audits and Accounts.-(1) the accounts of lhe university shall be maintained in suchform and in such manner as may be prescribed.
(2) the teaching departments, constituent colleges and institutes and all other bodiesdesignated as such by the syndicate in terms of statutes shafl be independent costcentre of the university with authority vested in the head ot each cost centre lo sanctionexpenditure out of lhe budget aflocated to it. provided that re-appropriation from onehead of expenditure to another may be made by the head of cost centre in accordancewlth and to the extent prescribed by the Statutes.(3) All funds generated by a teaching department, constituent co[ege or other unit of theuniversity through consultancy, research or other provision of service shall be madeavailable without prejudice to the budgetary allocauon othenrvise made, after deductionof overheads in the manner and to rhe extent prescribed by statute, to the teachingdepartment, constituent school or other unit for its development. A part of the funds sogenerated may be shared with the university teacher or research in charge of lheconsultancy, research or service concerned in the manner and to the extent pibscribedby Statute.
