CHAPTER VIIGENERAL PROVISIONS
36. Opportunity to show cause.' Except as otherwise provided by law no officer'teacher or other employee of the university holding a permanent post shall be reducedin rank, or removed or compulsorily retired from service for cause arising out of any a:tor omission on the part ofth" p"tton concerned unless he has been given a reasonableopportunity of showing cause against the action proposed to be laken'37. Appeal of the Syndicate and the Board of Governors'- Where an order ispassed punisning any officer (other than the RectoD, teacher or other employee of theUniversity or alerting or interpreting to his disadvantage the prescribed terms ofconditions of his service, he shall, whire the order is passed by any officer or teacher ofthe University other than the Rector, have the right to appeal to the Syndicate agairtstthe order, and where the order is passed by the Rector, have the right to appeal to llreBoard of Governors.38. Service of the University - (1) All persons employed by the University inaccordance with the terms and conditions of service prescribed by statutes shall 0epersons in the service of the University.(2) The academic and administrative staff of the university shall be selected wittt aview to achieve its stated objectives and the basic criteria for their selection shall be thehighest standards of competence, integrity, and efficiency.(3) ln case of academic staff, academic qualificalion and fringe benefits shall not beless than those duly approved by the Higher Education Commission (HEC) for sttchappointments.
