slatutes.3. Deans:There shall be a Dean of each faculty who shall be the Chairman and theconvenor of the Board of faculty. The dean of a faculty:' (i) Shatl be appointed by the Chancellor on the recommendations of theRector from amongst the three (03) seniors most Professors in theFaculty.For a term of three (03) years and shall be eligible for anotherterm.(iD Shall present candidates for admission to degrees, except honorarydegrees, to the Chancellor in the courses falling within the purview ofthe faculty.(iii) Shall exercise such powers and perform such duties as may beprescribed.4. Teaching Department:(a) There shall be a teaching department for each subject, or a group ofsubjects as may be prescribed by the regulations and each teachingdepartment shall be headed by Chairman.(b) The chairman of a teaching department shall be appointed by theBoard on the recommendation of the Rector from amongst the threemost senior Professors and three most senior Associate Probssors olthe department for a period ofthree years.(c) Provided that where there is no Professor or Associate professor in adepartment, it shall be looked after by the Dean of the facuhy with theassistance of the most senior teacher of the department.(d) Chairman of the Department shall plan, organize, and supervise thework of the department and shall be responsible to the Dean for thework of this department.5. Board of Studies:(1) There shall be a separate Board of Studies for each subject or group ofsubiects as may be prescribed by the regulations.(2) Each board of sludies shall consist of:
(i) The Chairman of the Department who shall act its Chairman andconveyor.(ii) All Professor and Associate Professors in lhe Department or thr:institutei(iii) Three teachers other than the University teachers to beappointed by the Faculty Board. The number will be determineCby the Faculty board according to the needs of each Board anc;(iv) Three experts to be appointed bythe Rector.
6. Function ofthe Board of Studies:(a) To advise the authorities on all academic matters connected wiihinstructions, research and examination in the subject or subjectsconcerned.
Page 32 of 34

endstream
